iding the auc of a cna  after size selection  by the auc of that same cna before size  selection  in addition to quantifying cnas see if  dna fragment length was also obtained  from paired and sequencing data  and finally after size selection the  cutoff size for each sample was  determined by calculating the point at  which the normalized recovery of the  sample  shifted from greater than 50 recovered  to less than 50 recovered  essentially marking the point at which  the gel electrophoresis was stopped and  the sample was extracted from the  collection filter  next i'm going to go through the results  from each of the five experiments  throughout this evaluation  and then some overall trends in the data  our first experiment was performed to  test the feasibility of using the your  jean health instruments for size  selection  and to evaluate the consistency of the  size selection  the figure on the top right shows the  proportion of total sequencing reads at  each fragment length between zero and  five hundred base pairs  the first question is in red and after  size selection is in blue  you can see that the size selection was  successful and the fragment length  profile after size selection has shifted  towards the smaller end  the figure on the bottom right shows the  proportion of fragment sizes less than  167 base pairs in yellow  and less than 150 base pairs in blue  before size selection is shown on the  left and after size selection on the  right  as expected before size selection we saw  about 50 of reeds below 167 base pairs  and about 25  below 150 base pairs  after size selection over 99 percent of  reads were below 167 base pairs and 97  below 150 base pairs  this sample set had an average size  selection cutoff of 141 base pairs and  the cutoff size cv was 3.7  these initial results were promising so  we wanted to add some additional samples  to our data set  sample set 2 was intended to increase  our sample size and gather additional  data  particula